---
title: logs_bloom (Osaka bloom.py)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> q_init
    q_init --> q_alloc : bloom = bytearray(256 zero bytes)
    q_alloc --> q_iter_logs : for log in logs
    q_iter_logs --> q_add_addr : has more logs
    q_add_addr --> q_iter_topics : add_to_bloom(bloom, log.address)
    q_iter_topics --> q_add_topic : has more topics
    q_add_topic --> q_iter_topics : add_to_bloom(bloom, topic)
    q_iter_topics --> q_iter_logs : no more topics
    q_iter_logs --> q_return : no more logs
    q_return --> q_final : return Bloom(bloom)
    q_final --> [*]

    note right of q_alloc
        INV: bloom is always a 256-byte
        bytearray throughout iteration
    end note

    note right of q_add_addr
        INV: every log.address is added
        to bloom exactly once
    end note

    note right of q_add_topic
        INV: every topic of every log is
        added to bloom exactly once
    end note

    note right of q_return
        INV: the returned Bloom is constructed
        from the fully populated bytearray
    end note
